<div class="crumb"><a href="https://dntavive.com/en">Home</a> / Ingredients</div><section class="section how-section" style="text-align:center"><div class="section-inner"><p class="s-tag center" style="color:#8BBC50">Ingredients</p><h1 class="s-heading center" style="color:#fff">DentaVive Ingredients: Five Probiotic Strains, a Mineral, and a Prebiotic Fiber</h1><p class="s-sub center" style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:0">A plain-language look at everything in the formula and the reason each ingredient was chosen.</p></div></section><section class="section "><div class="section-inner"><p class="s-tag center">The formula at a glance</p><h2 class="s-heading center">How the DentaVive Formula Is Built</h2><div class="quote-block" style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto"><p>DentaVive has two layers. The first is a five-strain probiotic culture, which supplies living bacteria associated with the mouth. The second is a mineral and fiber foundation: tricalcium phosphate for calcium and phosphate, and inulin to feed the probiotics.</p><p>Choosing several strains rather than one reflects how real microbiomes work, since a healthy community is diverse. Probiotic research is strain-specific, so findings on one strain do not automatically apply to another. We describe what each ingredient is and why it is included, and we avoid promising outcomes.</p></div><div class="callout-box" style="max-width:1000px;margin:10px auto 0">DentaVive is a dietary supplement that complements daily brushing, flossing, and regular dental visits. It is not a replacement for professional dental care.</div></div></section><section class="section ingr-section"><div class="section-inner"><p class="s-tag center">Ingredient by ingredient</p><h2 class="s-heading center">Every Ingredient Explained</h2><div class="ingr-grid one"><article class="ingr-card" style="align-items:flex-start"><div class="ingr-icon"><img src="/assets/images/Ingredients/Lactobacillus%20reuteri.png" alt="Lactobacillus reuteri in DentaVive" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="ingr-role">Probiotic Strain</div><h3 class="ingr-name" style="font-size:24px">Lactobacillus reuteri</h3><div class="ingr-desc"><p><i>L. reuteri</i> is a lactic acid bacterium that occurs naturally in the human body, including the mouth, and it is one of the better-researched probiotic species in oral-health science. In DentaVive it is the first of five strains chosen to help keep the oral community diverse and balanced.</p><p>Why it is here: a varied population of friendly bacteria leaves less room for less desirable species to dominate. Research on specific strains is ongoing, and results depend on the strain, the dose, and the person.</p></div></div></article><article class="ingr-card" style="align-items:flex-start"><div class="ingr-icon"><img src="/assets/images/Ingredients/Lactobacillus%20paracasei.png" alt="Lactobacillus paracasei in DentaVive" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="ingr-role">Probiotic Strain</div><h3 class="ingr-name" style="font-size:24px">Lactobacillus paracasei</h3><div class="ingr-desc"><p><i>L. paracasei</i> is a versatile species found in fermented foods and in the human body. It is included to widen the range of beneficial organisms in the formula instead of relying on a single strain.</p><p>Why it is here: diversity is a core principle of a healthy microbiome, and each strain in the blend plays a slightly different supporting role.</p></div></div></article><article class="ingr-card" style="align-items:flex-start"><div class="ingr-icon"><img src="/assets/images/Ingredients/Bifidobacterium%20lactis%20BL-04.png" alt="Bifidobacterium lactis BL-04 in DentaVive" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="ingr-role">Probiotic Strain</div><h3 class="ingr-name" style="font-size:24px">Bifidobacterium lactis BL-04</h3><div class="ingr-desc"><p><i>Bifidobacterium lactis</i> BL-04 is a documented commercial strain that is widely used in probiotic supplements. It broadens the blend beyond the lactobacilli and adds to the formula's overall bacterial diversity.</p><p>Why it is here: it helps complete a multi-strain culture designed to complement, not replace, daily brushing and flossing.</p></div></div></article><article class="ingr-card" style="align-items:flex-start"><div class="ingr-icon"><img src="/assets/images/Ingredients/Lactobacillus%20salivarius.png" alt="Lactobacillus salivarius in DentaVive" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="ingr-role">Probiotic Strain</div><h3 class="ingr-name" style="font-size:24px">Lactobacillus salivarius</h3><div class="ingr-desc"><p>As its name suggests, <i>L. salivarius</i> is a species associated with the saliva-rich environment of the mouth. It is one of the five strains included to support a healthier oral bacterial balance.</p><p>Why it is here: strains that belong to the oral environment are a logical choice for a formula built around the mouth.</p></div></div></article><article class="ingr-card" style="align-items:flex-start"><div class="ingr-icon"><img src="/assets/images/Ingredients/Streptococcus%20salivarius%20K12.png" alt="Streptococcus salivarius K12 in DentaVive" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="ingr-role">Probiotic Strain</div><h3 class="ingr-name" style="font-size:24px">Streptococcus salivarius K12</h3><div class="ingr-desc"><p><i>S. salivarius</i> K12 is one of the most widely studied oral probiotic strains and is often discussed in research on the mouth and throat microbiome.</p><p>Why it is here: it anchors the blend with a strain that has a substantial research history, while the other four strains add breadth.</p></div></div></article><article class="ingr-card" style="align-items:flex-start"><div class="ingr-icon"><img src="/assets/images/Ingredients/Tricalcium%20Phosphate.jpg" alt="Tricalcium Phosphate in DentaVive" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="ingr-role">Mineral Foundation</div><h3 class="ingr-name" style="font-size:24px">Tricalcium Phosphate</h3><div class="ingr-desc"><p>Tricalcium phosphate is a calcium phosphate mineral compound. Tooth enamel is made mostly of a related calcium phosphate mineral, which is why this ingredient is included as the mineral side of the formula.</p><p>Why it is here: calcium and phosphate are the building blocks of tooth structure, and the formula supplies them alongside the probiotic culture. It supports mineral intake and is not a substitute for fluoride, dental treatment, or professional care.</p></div></div></article><article class="ingr-card" style="align-items:flex-start"><div class="ingr-icon"><img src="/assets/images/Ingredients/insulin.jpg" alt="Inulin in DentaVive" loading="lazy"></div><div><div class="ingr-role">Prebiotic Fiber</div><h3 class="ingr-name" style="font-size:24px">Inulin</h3><div class="ingr-desc"><p>Inulin is a plant-based prebiotic fiber, meaning it is a food source for beneficial bacteria rather than a living organism itself. It is not insulin, the hormone, which is a common mix-up.</p><p>Why it is here: probiotics need something to feed on. Inulin is included to nourish the strains in the capsule, helping them settle in as part of your daily routine. People with sensitive digestion should start with the label serving and check with a healthcare professional if unsure.</p></div></div></article></div></div></section><section class="section "><div class="section-inner"><p class="s-tag center">Good to know</p><h2 class="s-heading center">Quality, Labels, and Safe Use</h2><div class="quote-block" style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto"><p><strong>Read the label.</strong> The Supplement Facts panel on your bottle is the authoritative source for amounts, serving size, allergens, and other ingredients.</p><p><strong>Start with your professional.</strong> If you are pregnant, nursing, immunocompromised, taking medication, or managing a condition, ask a doctor or pharmacist before starting any probiotic.</p><p><strong>Keep your dental routine.</strong> No capsule replaces brushing, flossing, or professional care.</p><p><strong>Store as directed.</strong> Follow the storage instructions on the bottle to protect the product.</p></div></div></section><section class="section faq-section"><div class="section-inner"><p class="s-tag center">Ingredient FAQ</p><h2 class="s-heading center">Ingredient Questions Answered</h2><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Which probiotic strains does DentaVive contain?<i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></button><div class="faq-answer">Lactobacillus reuteri, Lactobacillus paracasei, Bifidobacterium lactis BL-04, Lactobacillus salivarius, and Streptococcus salivarius K12.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Is the inulin in DentaVive the same as insulin?<i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></button><div class="faq-answer">No. Inulin is a plant-based prebiotic fiber. Insulin is a hormone and is not an ingredient in DentaVive.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Where can I find exact amounts per capsule?<i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></button><div class="faq-answer">Refer to the Supplement Facts panel on your bottle for exact amounts and the full list of other ingredients.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Can I take DentaVive if I have allergies or a health condition?<i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></button><div class="faq-answer">Check the label for allergen information and talk with a healthcare professional first, especially if you are pregnant, nursing, or taking medication.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">What does DentaVive contain besides probiotic strains?<i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></button><div class="faq-answer">Tricalcium phosphate, a calcium phosphate mineral, and inulin, a prebiotic fiber. Check the Supplement Facts panel for the full list of other ingredients.</div></div><div class="faq-item"><butt